    <text>
    <body>
        
        <div type="letter">
            <div type="text">
                <opener>
                    <placeName>Kew</placeName>
                    <date>April 7/75</date>
                    <salute>Dear Darwin</salute>
                </opener>
                <div type="transcription">
                     
<p>I like all the enclosed—but might you not add “&amp; the lower animals” where I have pencilled at the very end<ref target="#foot.f1"/></p>
<p>Ever aff y<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> | Jos D Hooker</p> 
                </div>
            </div>

            
            
        </div>

        

        

        <div type="footnotes">
            <note xml:id="foot.f1">Hooker refers to a draft petition to regulate vivisection (see <ref target="./DCP-LETT-9875.xml" resp="#mjhawkins">letter from T. H. Huxley, [4 April 1875]</ref> and n. 2).</note>
        </div>        
            
    </body>
